F$ through $S$ with respect to the upward-pointing unit normal vector $n.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421244 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4c6d18b-d618-53cd-9fce-a599b57a0c5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421244 #edb/ref 1074 "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nFor the surface $z=2$ for  $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1,$ the upward-pointing unit normal vector is\n\n$$\nn=⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=2$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨z,\\,y-x,\\,x+y⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,y-x,\\,x+y⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =x+y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+xy]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428947 #edb/ref 1030 0.3333333333333333 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428947 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 1 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.333333; nearest selected fraction = 1/3. Crossing activity numbers [3]; waits [3]. Separate account estimates: multivariable=1/3 (1/3). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage